# SM8250 additions on top of ROCKNIX's SM8250 config and kernel-common's
# steamos.config.

# AYANEO Pocket MICRO 2: panel and touchscreen (patches 0009 / 0010).
CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_AYANEO_AR18=m
CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_ST7123=m

# The ADSP firmware loads from the root, which is not mounted yet if the
# remoteproc driver is built in (ROCKNIX has it =y and nothing built-in
# firmware here). As a module it probes after switch_root.
CONFIG_QCOM_Q6V5_PAS=m

# Xiaomi Redmi K40 / POCO F3 (alioth): the Samsung AMS667XX01 DSC
# command-mode panel (patches/0017) and the FocalTech FT8756 SPI
# touchscreen (patches/0018).
#
# Built in, not =m like the panels above: alioth boots with no rootfs at
# all in phase 1, and the initramfs has no /lib/modules and no modprobe
# (kernel-common/initramfs/init only mounts the root and switch_roots).
# A console on the real panel is one of the two log channels there, so
# =m would mean a black screen with no way to find out why.
CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_SAMSUNG_AMS667XX01=y
CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_FT8756=y
# ... and the GENI SPI controller the touchscreen hangs off
# (/soc@0/geniqup@9c0000/spi@990000, &spi4) with it. A built-in touch
# driver on a modular bus has nothing to bind to.
CONFIG_SPI_QCOM_GENI=y

# alioth phase 1 debug channels (docs/alioth.md). ABL's splash
# framebuffer carries a console from the first seconds, before msm DRM
# probes: chosen/framebuffer@9c000000 in the DTS needs simpledrm to
# claim it.
CONFIG_DRM_SIMPLEDRM=y
# The USB gadget debug shell: kernel-common/initramfs/init brings up
# acm.usb0 (ACM serial) next to ncm.usb0, which is already =y here.
# U_SERIAL_CONSOLE is only offered once USB_U_SERIAL is on, which ACM
# selects -- it does not appear in the config at all without this.
CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_ACM=y
CONFIG_U_SERIAL_CONSOLE=y
# ramoops, with a verified address. The earlier note here said alioth's
# stock DTS has no ramoops region and left PSTORE_RAM at =m for want of
# an address -- that was wrong: the stock Android device tree reserves
# /reserved-memory/ramoops at <0x0 0xb0000000 0x0 0x00100000> and its
# kernel binds the driver there (b0000000.ramoops on the running phone).
# The DTS now carries that region, split to give a continuous console
# log as well as oops records.
#
# =y rather than =m for the same reason as the panel and touch drivers:
# phase 1 has no rootfs and no modprobe, and a crash log that needs a
# module loaded is no use to a kernel that dies during boot.
CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_PMSG=y

# USB-C host mode (a wired gamepad in the port). The FSA4480 is the SBU
# mux on &i2c15 at 0x42; alioth's DTS wires it to the PM8150B Type-C
# connector via mode-switch/orientation-switch plus the
# fsa4480_sbu_mux <-> pm8150b_typec_sbu_out endpoint pair.
#
# =m made the whole port dead, and not obviously: typec_register_port()
# calls typec_switch_get()/typec_mux_get() (drivers/usb/typec/class.c),
# which return -EPROBE_DEFER "when a connection was found but the switch
# has not been enumerated yet" (drivers/usb/typec/mux.c). With no rootfs
# there is no modprobe, so the mux is never enumerated, and
# c440000.spmi:pmic@2:typec@1500 sat in devices_deferred forever with an
# empty reason string -- no port, no role switching, no host mode. The
# repeated "Fixed dependency cycle(s)" lines around this connector are
# fw_devlink reporting cycles it already broke; they were not the cause.
#
# Measured on the phone: insmod'ing this exact module into the running
# =m kernel made /sys/class/typec/port0 appear at once, with
# port_type=[dual], data_role=host [device] and orientation=normal.
CONFIG_TYPEC_MUX_FSA4480=y

# Same failure mode, different victim: CONFIG_RTC_DRV_PM8XXX is already
# =y, but the PM8150 RTC takes its offset from the SDAM nvmem next door
# (/spmi@c440000/pmic@0/nvram@b100/rtc-offset@bc), so a modular SDAM
# leaves it deferred -- the running phone shows
# "c440000.spmi:pmic@0:rtc@6000 platform: wait for supplier
# .../rtc-offset@bc" and has no wall clock at all.
CONFIG_NVMEM_SPMI_SDAM=y

# Third time for the same failure mode, and the most expensive one: it
# cost the whole of WiFi and Bluetooth. The QCA6390 sits behind PCIe, and
# alioth's DTS describes it as a wifi@0 child of pcieport0 whose nine
# supplies come from the qca6390-pmu power sequencer. The PCI core turns
# such a DT child into a pwrctrl device and holds the host bridge until a
# driver claims it, because the chip has to be powered before the bus can
# be scanned. With the driver modular and no rootfs to modprobe it, the
# host bridge deferred forever -- devices_deferred read
# "1c00000.pcie  qcom-pcie: cannot initialize host" and
# /sys/bus/pci/devices was empty, which reads like dead PCIe hardware
# rather than a missing module.
#
# Measured on the phone, no reflash: insmod'ing this one 9.7KB module
# into the running =m kernel brought up 0000:00:00.0 and 0000:01:00.0
# (17cb:1101) immediately and emptied devices_deferred. With firmware
# reachable via firmware_class.path, ath11k_pci then found "qca6390
# hw2.0", read back fw_version 0x10121492, and created wlan0; hci_uart
# brought up hci0 over &uart6 after downloading qca/htbtfw20.tlv.
#
# Deliberately NOT set here, and this is the interesting part. The
# obvious fix is CONFIG_PCI_PWRCTRL_PWRSEQ=y, by analogy with the two
# entries above. Kconfig refuses it, and the build says so:
#
#   WARN CONFIG_PCI_PWRCTRL_PWRSEQ=y not applied (got: ...=m)
#
# PCI_PWRCTRL_PWRSEQ is a hidden tristate with no prompt
# (drivers/pci/pwrctrl/Kconfig); its value comes from
# "select PCI_PWRCTRL_PWRSEQ if HAVE_PWRCTRL" in ath11k's Kconfig, so it
# tracks ATH11K_PCI. The only way to y is ATH11K_PCI=y -- and that would
# break phase 2 rather than help it: ath11k requests
# ath11k/QCA6390/hw2.0/amss.bin at probe, which is in the rootfs, which
# is not mounted yet when a built-in driver probes.
#
# Left modular because the gap is phase-1-only and closes by
# construction. Measured, not assumed: insmod'ing the module into the
# running kernel retried the deferred 1c00000.pcie probe and the bus came
# up at once, so load order does not matter -- whenever udev gets to it
# in phase 2, PCIe follows. ATH11K and BT stay modular for the same
# reason plus firmware timing.
#
# What phase 2 must check: that something actually loads this module.
# Nothing else depends on it, so if the QCA6390 is missing from the bus
# there, look here first.

# --- Audio: the two CS35L41 speaker amps ---------------------------------
#
# alioth has no WCD938x and no WSA881x -- nothing like the handhelds. Its
# only audio path is two Cirrus CS35L41 amps on i2c3 (speaker-amp@40 and
# @41, prefixes RCV and LCV), fed by TERTIARY_TDM_RX_0. They are the sole
# codec of the sound card's only codec link:
#
#   speaker-dai-link { codec { sound-dai = <&cs35l41_rcv 0>, <&cs35l41_lcv 0>; }; }
#
# ROCKNIX leaves both CS35L41_I2C and CS35L41_SPI unset, because none of
# the handhelds use this part. Without the driver the codec components
# never register, qcom,sm8250-sndcard never finishes binding its DAI link,
# and **the card never appears at all** -- not "speakers are silent",
# no /dev/snd/controlC0, no UCM, nothing for PipeWire to open. The symptom
# is a long way from the cause, which is why it gets a comment this long.
#
# =m, not =y: userspace loads it from modules-load.d/alioth.conf in
# phase 2, and the amp's tuning firmware lives in the rootfs.
CONFIG_SND_SOC_CS35L41_I2C=m

# 把 dev_dbg() 留成可以在真机上打开的东西。TDM 配置转储（q6afe-dai.c）是
# 定位「ADSP 回一个不分型的 EBADPARAM」的唯一手段 —— 那次排查里 dev_dbg 被
# 编译掉了，只好临时改成 dev_info 再重编一轮内核。开着它，下次直接：
#   echo 'file q6afe-dai.c +p' > /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control
CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG=y

# =========================================================================
# OnePlus 8 Pro (instantnoodlep) — 本段只对这一台设备有意义，但整段写进
# 共享的 config 是无害的：上面 alioth 的 AMS667XX01 / FT8756 / CS35L41
# 对 OnePlus 同样无害，反过来也一样。多编进去几个驱动只花几百 KB。
#
# 依据全部是 2026-10-25 在这台机器上实测的（docs/op8p/README.md）：
#   DTS: external-and-mods/kernel-sm8250/dts/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodlep.dts
# =========================================================================

# --- 触摸：Samsung S6SY761 -----------------------------------------------
#
# 实测 /sys/bus/i2c/devices/4-0048 -> sec-s6sy761，chip-name SY79x，
# 17x38 TX/RX，1440x3168，irq=tlmm 39、reset=tlmm 38。
#
# 和 alioth 的 FT8756 一样是 "=y 而不是 =m"：阶段 1 没有 rootfs、没有
# modprobe，=m 在这个阶段等于不存在，而触摸是阶段 1 要验收的外设之一。
# ROCKNIX 默认 # CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_S6SY761 is not set，所以这里必须显式打开。
#
# 总线是 I2C（i2c@a94000，走 QUPv3），不是 SPI —— 所以不需要
# CONFIG_SPI_QCOM_GENI 那一条（那是 alioth 的 FT8756 才要的）。
CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_S6SY761=y

# --- 显示：三星 ANA6706（DSI0，DSC 命令模式）-----------------------------
#
# panel-name "samsung ana6706 dsc cmd mode panel"，4 组时序
# （1080x2376@60/120、1440x3168@60/120），cmdline 选择器是
# msm_drm.dsi_display0=qcom,mdss_dsi_samsung_ana6706_dsc_cmd。
#
# 驱动本身在 mainline 里**不存在**，要自己写（参考 alioth 的 patch 0017
# 的移植方法）。驱动落地之前这里不要加一行 CONFIG_ —— Kconfig 里没有
# 这个符号，build.sh 会打 "WARN ... not applied"，那只是个噪音，
# 但更糟的是它会让人以为面板已经准备好了。
#
# 在面板驱动落地之前，显示靠 DTS 里的 chosen/framebuffer@9c000000
# （cont_splash_region，实测 size 0x2300000）由 simpledrm 接管，
# 也就是 CONFIG_DRM_SIMPLEDRM=y（上面已有）。这足够阶段 1 看控制台。

# --- 音频：这里没有一项是为 OnePlus 准备的 ------------------------------
#
# 实测拓扑：wcd938x_codec + bolero，扬声器是两颗 nxp,tfa98xx（I2C，
# reset tlmm 91/99），qcom,wsa-max-devs = 0（没有 WSA881x）。
#
# **不要**在这里加 CONFIG_SND_SOC_TFA98XX：mainline 没有这个符号，
# 驱动要从 NXP 的 out-of-tree 移植（约 2500 行），是一个独立的任务。
# 上面 alioth 那条 CONFIG_SND_SOC_CS35L41_I2C=m 对 OnePlus 无害也无用
# （它的 DTS 里没有 CS35L41 节点，组件不会注册）。

# --- 显示：ANA6706 面板驱动（patches/0029）-------------------------------
#
# =y 而不是 =m，同上面 S6SY761 的理由：阶段 1 没有 rootfs、没有 modprobe，
# =m 在这个阶段等于不存在，而面板控制台是阶段 1 的两条日志通道之一。
#
# DCS 初始化序列和 timing@1 的完整 DSC PPS 都已从本机 DT 转录进 0029。
# 配置的 RC 参数与该 PPS 必须完全一致：DPU 从 drm_dsc_config 编码，面板
# 从 0x9e 命令解码；两边有一处不同都会表现为花屏或黑屏。
CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_ONEOPLUS_ANA6706=y
